fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.33.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 3.33.1, with fixes for 11 security advisories
    (GHSA-x863-43r4-f7c2, GHSA-m33m-4qxh-hq76, GHSA-52rf-pppx-qm55,
    GHSA-3664-pr8r-3254, GHSA-rp99-f9qv-c446, GHSA-23fv-6wrf-5hfq,
    GHSA-f6v9-vx5q-vjpf, GHSA-m6hp-4798-x78x, GHSA-9c9j-2r7q-5gx2,
    GHSA-ch3p-5r9r-w86p, GHSA-76c4-7552-ffhv).
  * patches/freerdp: 0009 (WLog journald appender) dropped, fixed upstream
    (ba36e42a1d: WINPR_HAVE_JOURNALD_H is now a private compile definition
    of libwinpr). 0001-0008 still needed and apply unchanged (0004 and
    0005 only moved).
  * build-freerdp.sh checks the journald appender in libwinpr3 itself,
    since config.h no longer carries WINPR_HAVE_JOURNALD_H.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:00:24 +0100

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.33.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 3.33.0, with fixes for 13 security advisories
    (GHSA-hhfh-fvm7-7w65, GHSA-pq35-c472-69w2, GHSA-v7hr-xh82-79p7,
    GHSA-9r9q-9r7p-4mr6, GHSA-76c4-7552-ffhv, GHSA-j5pq-cm28-qm6v,
    GHSA-2hm9-2h5q-x525, GHSA-hj6g-r86h-wrcg, GHSA-fw6x-h8gw-778w,
    GHSA-q8p6-8mmj-j4ph, GHSA-r664-f94r-rgg6, GHSA-4g67-jhpc-q5xp,
    GHSA-8m87-jj8p-2fqc).
  * patches/freerdp: all nine still needed; 0008 refreshed (new context in
    peer.c), the others only moved.
  * Upstream changes the fastrdp proxy module sees: fast-path input before
    activation is dropped (#13889; the module's SelfRedirect relied on it
    and is removed); the Disconnect Provider Ultimatum carries the reason
    it is sent with (#13873, "provider initiated" instead of always "user
    requested"); the proxy forwards input and Refresh Rect / Suppress
    Output through its client thread (#13896).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:23:06 +0100

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.32.2-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * patches/freerdp: core/peer (0007): a reactivation that the peer's
    PostConnect starts and reads itself no longer ends in a failed read:
    the state machine's rerun after the client's Font List PDU no longer
    parses the consumed stream again (FreeRDP logged a tpkt "got 0" warning
    with a backtrace and a transport_check_fds error). The fastrdp proxy
    module's lab switch WaitingScreenReactivate does this (backlog A5).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:14:56 +0100

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.32.2-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * patches/freerdp: core/peer: a client's Shutdown Request PDU (mstsc: the X
    in its connection bar) is answered with a Shutdown Request Denied PDU once
    PostConnect accepted the client, and the client disconnects itself
    ([MS-RDPBCGR] 1.3.1.4.1); before that the connection is still closed at
    once. Until now the server always disconnected with "provider initiated".
  * patches/freerdp: winpr/wlog: WITH_SYSTEMD now reaches winpr/config.h, so
    WLOG_APPENDER=JOURNALD selects the journald appender (it was compiled but
    unreachable). Build with -DWITH_SYSTEMD=ON (was the non-existent
    WITH_LIBSYSTEMD) and fail the build without the appender.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:32:42 +0200

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.32.2-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * patches/freerdp: core/peer: a PDU read while the peer's PostConnect runs
    (the callback reads the connection itself) is handled as input of the
    active connection instead of running PostConnect a second time;
    freerdp_peer_in_post_connect() tells the callback. The fastrdp proxy
    module's desktop picker reads keys and clicks that way.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:47:57 +0200

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.32.2-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * patches/freerdp: server/proxy: drop a back-end's Server Status Info PDU
    instead of forwarding it when the front client did not announce
    RNS_UD_CS_SUPPORT_STATUSINFO_PDU ([MS-RDPBCGR] 3.3.5.7.2).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:08:43 +0200

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.32.2-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * patches/freerdp: winpr/kerberos: the Kerberos acceptor keeps what the KDC
    asserted in the accepted ticket and offers it as context attributes:
    authentication indicators from a CAMMAC whose svc-verifier checks out
    (SECPKG_ATTR_KERBEROS_AUTH_INDICATORS) and the PAC_LOGON_INFO of a PAC
    whose server signature verifies (SECPKG_ATTR_KERBEROS_PAC_LOGON_INFO).
    The fastrdp proxy module passes them to the broker, which can count them
    as the second factor per login ([mfa] kdc_evidence_as_mfa).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:26:06 +0200

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.32.2-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * patches/freerdp: winpr/kerberos: the Kerberos user-to-user acceptor answers
    with the TGT of the machine account (<NAME>$ in the keytab) before trying
    the service principal itself. Windows clients (mstsc under CredSSP) start
    with user-to-user; with Active Directory the KDC refuses TERMSRV/<host> as
    an AS client, so Kerberos NLA from Windows always failed.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:32:32 +0200

fastrdp-freerdp3 (3.32.2-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * patches/freerdp: core/nego: answer a Remote Credential Guard request the
    server does not support with an RDP_NEG_RSP without
    REDIRECTED_AUTHENTICATION_MODE_SUPPORTED instead of dropping the TCP
    connection (mstsc /remoteGuard).
  * patches/freerdp: core/nla: accept TSRemoteGuardCreds without the optional
    supplementalCreds (FreeRDP clients never send them).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:49:57 +0200

